<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>In the expansion of <m>(1 + kx)^{6}</m>, where <m>k</m> is a positive number, the coefficient of <m>x^{2}</m> is <m>{240}</m>. Find <m>k</m>.</p><div><m>k =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Number <m>{2}</m> of the row for power <m>{6}</m> is <m>{15}</m>, so the term in <m>x^{2}</m> is <m>{15}(kx)^{2} = {15}k^{2}x^{2}</m>.</p><p><me>{15}k^{2} = {240} \quad\Rightarrow\quad k^{2} = {16} \quad\Rightarrow\quad k = {4}</me></p><p>The square root could also be <m>{-4}</m>, but <m>k</m> is positive, so <m>k = {4}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>